# Cloudflare Pages path-level redirects and rewrites (first matching rule wins).
# Note: Hostname-level redirects (www.slatico.dev -> https://slatico.dev) must be configured
# via a Cloudflare Zone-Level Redirect Rule (http.host eq "www.slatico.dev") to preserve paths
# and query strings without causing a path-wildcard loop on the apex domain.
/home / 301
/explore /icons 301
/documentation /docs 301

# Icon Explorer deep links. Pages applies these rules BEFORE serving static files, so:
# 1. Next.js's own /icons route data (/icons/__next*.txt, /icons/__next.icons/...) must pass
#    through untouched (rewriting a path to itself serves the real file, or a 404 if missing).
# 2. /icons/<slug>/ (trailing slash) is normalised to /icons/<slug>.
# 3. /icons/<slug> (exactly one segment) is served the /icons page with HTTP 200 and an unchanged
#    URL; the Explorer validates the slug against the catalog and opens the detail drawer.
# Nothing except Next.js `__next*` files may be emitted under out/icons/ (enforced by
# scripts/verify-website-export.ts), or it would be shadowed by rule 3.
/icons/__next* /icons/__next:splat 200
/icons/:slug/ /icons/:slug 301
/icons/:slug /icons 200
